            <article class="article-body fs-6 lh-lg">
                <p class="lead">September has been the busiest trophy month the forex industry has seen in years. Within eight days, two separate ceremonies — one in Limassol, one in Dubai — handed out honours to some of the biggest names in retail and institutional trading. The names differed. The categories were strikingly similar. And the pattern they form is worth reading closely, because it says a lot about what traders and judges actually value right now.</p>

                <h2 class="mt-5 mb-3">Limassol: FP Markets takes three at the Global Forex Awards</h2>

                <p>On 15 September, the <strong>Global Forex Awards 2026</strong> held its eighth annual ceremony at the Amara Hotel in Limassol, Cyprus. <strong>FP Markets</strong> walked away with three distinctions: <strong>'Best Value Broker – Global'</strong>, <strong>'Most Transparent Broker – Asia'</strong> and <strong>'Most Transparent Broker – Latam'</strong>.</p>

                <p>It is worth pausing on those categories. 'Best Value Broker' is not a vague popularity crown — it is a public vote on the economics of trading: spreads, costs, conditions. And 'Most Transparent Broker' in two regions is the kind of double that can only come from clients, not a judges' panel, since these wins were decided by vote. As the broker's Chief Marketing Officer John Lewis put it: "In an industry where competition is intense, being voted Best Value Broker globally, alongside Most Transparent Broker in both Asia and Latam, is a reflection of what our clients experience day to day."</p>

                <p>FP Markets is no overnight success story — it was established in Sydney in 2005, is headquartered in Limassol, offers more than 10,000 CFD instruments across seven asset classes on MetaTrader 4/5, TradingView and cTrader, and holds licences from ASIC, the FSA in Seychelles, South Africa's FSCA and Kenya's CMA. With more than 80 awards to its name, the Limassol triple was another line in a long record — but the <em>categories</em> are the real story.</p>

                <h2 class="mt-5 mb-3">Dubai: MultiBank Group doubles up at Forex Expo Dubai</h2>

                <p>One week later, the awards stage moved to the Dubai World Trade Centre. During <a href="{{ url('/forex-expo-dubai-2026') }}">Forex Expo Dubai 2026</a> — the record-breaking ninth edition we covered earlier this week — <strong>MultiBank Group</strong> collected two awards: <strong>'Best Global Institutional Financial Ecosystem of the Year'</strong> and <strong>'Excellence in Global Financial Markets Innovation and Community Impact'</strong>.</p>

                <p>The first recognised the breadth of the group's institutional offering — trading, liquidity, technology, infrastructure, execution, market access and tailored client solutions under one roof. The second acknowledged its investment in market innovation alongside contributions to financial education, accessibility and industry development.</p>

                <p>"We are honoured to receive these two awards at Forex Expo Dubai 2026," said Founder and Chairman Naser Taher. "Since our establishment in 2005, we have remained focused on delivering reliable solutions for clients across global markets while contributing positively to the continued development of the financial services industry." Two decades old, multi-regulated, and winning in institutional categories — MultiBank's double fits the same pattern as FP Markets' triple, just at the institutional end of the market.</p>

                <h2 class="mt-5 mb-3">The pattern: checkable traits beat shiny claims</h2>

                <p>Step back and look at what both ceremonies actually rewarded. In Limassol: value and transparency. In Dubai: ecosystem strength and innovation with community impact. None of these are awards you win with a marketing budget alone. 'Most Transparent Broker' voted by clients in two regions requires years of consistent behaviour. 'Best Global Institutional Financial Ecosystem' requires infrastructure you can inspect. 'Community Impact' requires a record of actually doing things — education, accessibility, industry development.</p>

                <p>Compare that with the era — not so long ago — when 'Best Broker' titles floated around with little behind them beyond a sponsorship cheque. The industry has moved on, and awards have had to move with it. Traders in 2026 have seen enough broker failures, enough opaque fee structures and enough empty 'best' claims to reward something harder to fake: <strong>measurable traits</strong>. Pricing you can compare. Disclosures you can read. Infrastructure you can verify.</p>

                <p>That is a healthy development for the awards industry as a whole — and it raises the bar for every programme running this year, ours included. When recognition has to be earned in public, on numbers traders can check, the trophies start meaning something again.</p>

                <h2 class="mt-5 mb-3">Two cities, two audiences, one direction</h2>

                <p>It is also worth noting who was in each room. Limassol's ceremony spoke to the global retail trading world — the clients and partners whose votes decided the outcome. Dubai's expo floor spoke to the industry's business side — the institutions, IBs and affiliates building the region's trading infrastructure. That both audiences, independently, landed on value, transparency and genuine ecosystem strength says this is not a fashion. It is the direction of travel.</p>

                <h2 class="mt-5 mb-3">Why this matters for the ProFX Awards</h2>

                <p>The September results validate the direction the serious awards programmes have been taking: fewer vanity categories, more judged and voted recognition for the things traders can actually check. When we open nominations, we ask the industry to name the brokers and fintech brands that deliver — on value, on transparency, on genuine service — not the ones with the loudest booths.</p>

                <p>The message from Limassol and Dubai is clear: 2026 rewards substance. Nominations for <strong>ProFX Awards {{ Helper::awardYear() }}</strong> are open, and the ceremony takes place on {{ Helper::awardEventDate() }} in Dubai. If you know a broker, fintech company or trading provider whose value and transparency deserve industry-wide recognition, <a href="{{ url('/nomination') }}">submit a nomination</a> — the categories this year are built for exactly that.</p>
